  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0073, and it contains five tables. The first table is Insurance_Agent, which stores information about insurance agents, including their contact phone number, hire date, and name. The second table is Customer, which stores information about customers, including their contact phone number, customer ID, ID card number, and name. The third table is Payment_Record, which stores information about payment records, including the payment amount, payment method, payment time, policy ID, and foreign key references to the Insurance_Policy table. The fourth table is Insurance_Policy, which stores information about insurance policies, including the agent ID, customer ID, insurance term, insurance type, insured amount, policy ID, premium, and foreign key references to the Insurance_Agent and Customer tables. The fifth table is Claim_Record, which stores information about claim records, including the claim amount, claim time, policy ID, and foreign key reference to the Payment_Record table. The primary keys for each table are listed in parentheses. The foreign keys are listed in parentheses and reference the primary key of the referenced table. The update and delete rules for each foreign key are also listed.",
  "gold_question": "The insurance company has multiple insurance agents, each with a unique Agent ID, Name, Hire Date, and Contact Phone Number. An agent can handle insurance business for multiple customers. Each customer has a Customer ID, Name, ID Card Number, and Contact Phone Number. Each insurance policy has a unique Policy Number, Insurance Type (Life, Health, Property), Insured Amount, Insurance Term, and Premium. Each premium payment requires recording the Payment Amount, Payment Time, and Payment Method. In addition, the insurance company needs to keep track of each customer's Claim Records.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0073.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0073\nCREATE TABLE `insurance_agent` (\n  `agent_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_phone` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `hire_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`agent_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_phone` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `id_card_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `insurance_policy` (\n  `policy_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `agent_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `insurance_term` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `insurance_type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `insured_amount` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `premium` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`policy_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `insurance_policy_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`agent_id`) REFERENCES `insurance_agent` (`agent_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `insurance_policy_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `payment_record` (\n  `payment_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `policy_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `payment_amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `payment_method` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `payment_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`payment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `payment_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`policy_id`) REFERENCES `insurance_policy` (`policy_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `claim_record` (\n  `claim_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `policy_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `claim_amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `claim_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`claim_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `claim_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`policy_id`) REFERENCES `payment_record` (`payment_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
